  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186087699,
      "id": "9b9ef325-2358-5041-8a8d-b459e8ed9f09",
      "title": "Determining the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "1eddb0a6-f472-5168-a694-dd2b7bf675e6",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3} & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $AB=BA={I}_{2}$\n- **II.** $AC=CA={I}_{2}$\n- **III.** $B={A}^{-1}$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- First, we check whether $AB=BA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\u2217 & \u2217 \\\\ \u2217 & -6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{2}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is false. As a result, $B\\ne {A}^{-1}$ and statement III is false too.\n\n- Now, we check whether $AC=CA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3} & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $CA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CA & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3} & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\".",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "5088018f-32e5-5785-b92e-ed8490dca969",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
